<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>AI Literacy Series — The Map</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f7f7f5;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --ink: #1a1a1a;
    --ink-soft: #55554f;
    --ink-faint: #8a8a80;
    --line: #e6e6e0;
    --accent: #2f6d5b;
    --accent-soft: #e6f0ec;
    --lens: #7a4f1d;
    --lens-soft: #f7ede0;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.04), 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.05);
    --radius: 14px;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #121312;
      --surface: #1c1e1c;
      --ink: #ecece7;
      --ink-soft: #b4b4ac;
      --ink-faint: #7d7d75;
      --line: #2c2f2c;
      --accent: #6bbfa4;
      --accent-soft: #1b2b26;
      --lens: #d6a86a;
      --lens-soft: #2a2016;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3), 0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px) clamp(18px, 4vw, 40px) 64px; }

  header.masthead { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .09em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 44px); line-height: 1.08; font-weight: 760;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 14px; max-width: 20ch;
  }
  .dek { font-size: clamp(15px, 2.2vw, 17.5px); color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; max-width: 60ch; }
  .dek strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 620; }

  /* editorial lens banner */
  .lens {
    display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start;
    background: var(--lens-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 16px 20px; margin: 34px 0 8px;
  }
  .lens .mark {
    flex: none; width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 8px;
    display: grid; place-items: center; background: var(--lens); color: #fff;
    font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 1px;
  }
  .lens .body { font-size: 14.5px; }
  .lens .body b { color: var(--lens); font-weight: 680; letter-spacing: .01em; }
  .lens .body span { color: var(--ink-soft); display: block; margin-top: 2px; }

  .rail {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin: 40px 0 22px;
    color: var(--ink-faint); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .rail::after { content: ""; flex: 1; height: 1px; background: var(--line); }

  .grid {
    display: grid; gap: 18px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);
  }
  /* top row: themes 1-3 each span two of six columns (3-up) */
  .grid > .card:nth-child(-n+3) { grid-column: span 2; }
  /* bottom row: themes 4-5 each span three of six columns (2-up) */
  .grid > .card:nth-child(n+4) { grid-column: span 3; }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .grid > .card { grid-column: auto !important; }
    .grid > .card:nth-child(-n+3):last-child,
    .grid > .card:nth-child(4) { grid-column: 1 / -1 !important; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .grid > .card { grid-column: auto !important; }
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 22px 22px 8px; box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  }
  .card > .head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .num {
    flex: none; width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 9px;
    display: grid; place-items: center; font-weight: 730; font-size: 15px;
    background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent);
  }
  .card h2 { font-size: 17.5px; font-weight: 680; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0; line-height: 1.2; }

  ol.points { list-style: none; counter-reset: p; margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 0; }
  ol.points li {
    counter-increment: p; position: relative; padding: 9px 0 9px 30px;
    font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  ol.points li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  ol.points li::before {
    content: counter(p); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 9px;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink-faint);
    width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid; place-items: center; line-height: 1;
  }
  ol.points li b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 640; }
  ol.points li .note { color: var(--ink-faint); }

  .aside {
    margin-top: 26px; border: 1px dashed var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 16px 20px; background: transparent;
    display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .aside .tag {
    flex: none; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .07em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; padding: 4px 11px;
  }
  .aside .txt { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .aside .txt b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 620; }

  footer.foot {
    margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-faint); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <header class="masthead">
    <p class="eyebrow">AI-literacy series · Swedish · free · no sponsors</p>
    <h1>What everyone should actually understand about AI</h1>
    <p class="dek"><strong>Episode 1 is this whole map</strong> — one brief pass over every theme below. Each theme then becomes its own deep-dive later. The goal isn't to cover the news; it's to leave you able to judge it.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="lens">
    <div class="mark">!</div>
    <div class="body">
      <b>The lens over everything: cut through the noise.</b>
      <span>AI attracts a flood of money- and fear-driven voices. Most mean well; few add clarity. Every topic here is delivered to reduce confusion, not add to it.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="rail">The five themes</div>

  <div class="grid">

    <section class="card">
      <div class="head"><div class="num">1</div><h2>What AI actually is</h2></div>
      <ol class="points">
        <li><b>“AI” is just the everyday word</b> for today's tools — no jargon needed.</li>
        <li>You judge it by <b>what you observe when using it</b>, not by theory.</li>
        <li><b>“It's just autocomplete” is a comforting rationalization</b> — assume it keeps improving.</li>
        <li>It keeps getting smarter at concrete things: <b>execution, reasoning, orchestration</b>.</li>
        <li><b>Emergent capability</b> — complex behavior arises from simple primitives.</li>
        <li>Open vs. closed models. <span class="note">(the one distinction worth knowing)</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <div class="head"><div class="num">2</div><h2>Where it already touches your life</h2></div>
      <ol class="points">
        <li><b>AI you already use</b> without realizing it.</li>
        <li>Generative tools: <b>real uses, real limits</b>.</li>
        <li>AI at work: <b>automation vs. augmentation</b>.</li>
        <li>The breadth — use cases across the <b>whole spectrum</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <div class="head"><div class="num">3</div><h2>The risks</h2></div>
      <ol class="points">
        <li><b>Privacy</b> — what happens to what you type.</li>
        <li><b>Scams &amp; fraud</b>, now AI-enabled.</li>
        <li><b>Deepfakes &amp; misinformation</b>.</li>
        <li><b>Bias</b> in automated decisions.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <div class="head"><div class="num">4</div><h2>What stays human — and what you'll need</h2></div>
      <ol class="points">
        <li><b>Human vs. AI capability trajectory</b> — where each is ahead, and where the curves are heading.</li>
        <li><b>Wave 1 → Wave 2:</b> from replacing solo tasks to orchestrating swarms of agents — the collaboration frontier.</li>
        <li><b>Any “what's still needed?” answer needs a time horizon</b> — meaningful to ~24 months, guesswork beyond.</li>
        <li><b>Prompt engineering is dying</b> — being explicit matters less; taste and judgment on what's <em>correct</em> matter more.</li>
        <li><b>Core human traits to lean into:</b> connection, clarity, and being <em>more</em> technically enabled.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <div class="head"><div class="num">5</div><h2>The big picture — society &amp; power</h2></div>
      <ol class="points">
        <li><b>Jobs &amp; the economy</b> — hype vs. realistic.</li>
        <li><b>Who controls this</b>, and why it matters.</li>
        <li><b>The EU AI Act</b> — what it actually means for you.</li>
        <li><b>The AGI / superintelligence debate.</b></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

  </div>

  <div class="aside">
    <span class="tag">On demand</span>
    <span class="txt"><b>Glossary teaser</b> — model, product, MCP, skills, API, CLI. A separate video, made only if people ask for it.</span>
  </div>

  <footer class="foot">
    <span>The map = Episode 1. Themes 1–5 read top to bottom, concrete → speculative.</span>
    <span>Series overview</span>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
